  "raw_response": "```python\nfrom collections import deque\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef solve(grid: List[List[int]]) -> List[List[int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Transform a grid that contains only 0 and 3.\n    Each orthogonal connected component of 3 is replaced by a new value:\n        \u2022 2  \u2013 if any cell of the component has more than two neighbours\n               (i.e. a branching node, degree \u2265 3)\n        \u2022 6  \u2013 else if the component contains more than one \"bend\"\n               (a degree\u20112 cell whose two neighbours are orthogonal)\n        \u2022 1  \u2013 otherwise (simple path or a single bend)\n    All original 0 cells stay 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    visited = [[False] * cols for _ in range(rows)]\n    out = [[0] * cols for _ in range(rows)]\n\n    # directions: up, down, left, right\n    dirs = [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]\n\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] != 3 or visited[r][c]:\n                continue\n\n            # BFS to collect whole component\n            comp = []\n            q = deque()\n            q.append((r, c))\n            visited[r][c] = True\n            while q:\n                cr, cc = q.popleft()\n                comp.append((cr, cc))\n                for dr, dc in dirs:\n                    nr, nc = cr + dr, cc + dc\n                    if 0 <= nr < rows and 0 <= nc < cols:\n                        if not visited[nr][nc] and grid[nr][nc] == 3:\n                            visited[nr][nc] = True\n                            q.append((nr, nc))\n\n            # analyse the component\n            comp_set = set(comp)\n            max_deg = 0\n            bends = 0\n\n            for (cr, cc) in comp:\n                # count neighbours inside the component\n                deg = 0\n                neigh = []\n                for dr, dc in dirs:\n                    nr, nc = cr + dr, cc + dc\n                    if 0 <= nr < rows and 0 <= nc < cols and (nr, nc) in comp_set:\n                        deg += 1\n                        neigh.append((nr, nc))\n                if deg > max_deg:\n                    max_deg = deg\n\n                # detect a bend: degree exactly 2 and neighbours not aligned\n                if deg == 2:\n                    r1, c1 = neigh[0]\n                    r2, c2 = neigh[1]\n                    # aligned if same row or same column\n                    if r1 != r2 and c1 != c2:\n                        bends += 1\n\n            # decide the label\n            if max_deg >= 3:\n                label = 2\n            elif bends > 1:\n                label = 6\n            else:\n                label = 1\n\n            # write the label into the output\n            for (cr, cc) in comp:\n                out[cr][cc] = label\n\n    return out\n```",
  "script": "from collections import deque\nfrom typing import List\n\ndef solve(grid: List[List[int]]) -> List[List[int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Transform a grid that contains only 0 and 3.\n    Each orthogonal connected component of 3 is replaced by a new value:\n        \u2022 2  \u2013 if any cell of the component has more than two neighbours\n               (i.e. a branching node, degree \u2265 3)\n        \u2022 6  \u2013 else if the component contains more than one \"bend\"\n               (a degree\u20112 cell whose two neighbours are orthogonal)\n        \u2022 1  \u2013 otherwise (simple path or a single bend)\n    All original 0 cells stay 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not grid:\n        return []\n\n    rows = len(grid)\n    cols = len(grid[0])\n    visited = [[False] * cols for _ in range(rows)]\n    out = [[0] * cols for _ in range(rows)]\n\n    # directions: up, down, left, right\n    dirs = [(-1, 0), (1, 0), (0, -1), (0, 1)]\n\n    for r in range(rows):\n        for c in range(cols):\n            if grid[r][c] != 3 or visited[r][c]:\n                continue\n\n            # BFS to collect whole component\n            comp = []\n            q = deque()\n            q.append((r, c))\n            visited[r][c] = True\n            while q:\n                cr, cc = q.popleft()\n                comp.append((cr, cc))\n                for dr, dc in dirs:\n                    nr, nc = cr + dr, cc + dc\n                    if 0 <= nr < rows and 0 <= nc < cols:\n                        if not visited[nr][nc] and grid[nr][nc] == 3:\n                            visited[nr][nc] = True\n                            q.append((nr, nc))\n\n            # analyse the component\n            comp_set = set(comp)\n            max_deg = 0\n            bends = 0\n\n            for (cr, cc) in comp:\n                # count neighbours inside the component\n                deg = 0\n                neigh = []\n                for dr, dc in dirs:\n                    nr, nc = cr + dr, cc + dc\n                    if 0 <= nr < rows and 0 <= nc < cols and (nr, nc) in comp_set:\n                        deg += 1\n                        neigh.append((nr, nc))\n                if deg > max_deg:\n                    max_deg = deg\n\n                # detect a bend: degree exactly 2 and neighbours not aligned\n                if deg == 2:\n                    r1, c1 = neigh[0]\n                    r2, c2 = neigh[1]\n                    # aligned if same row or same column\n                    if r1 != r2 and c1 != c2:\n                        bends += 1\n\n            # decide the label\n            if max_deg >= 3:\n                label = 2\n            elif bends > 1:\n                label = 6\n            else:\n                label = 1\n\n            # write the label into the output\n            for (cr, cc) in comp:\n                out[cr][cc] = label\n\n    return out",
